@startuml
' Discivium proposed component architecture

title Discivium - Proposed Component Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor Student
actor Lecturer

package "Discivium Django application" {
  component "Shared presentation\nand configuration" as Presentation
  component "Identity and access" as Identity
  component "Courses and enrollment" as Courses
  component Learning

  package "Future modules" #F5F5F5 {
    component "Academic record" as AcademicRecord #DDDDDD
    component Registration #DDDDDD
    component Finance #DDDDDD
    component "Student services" as StudentServices #DDDDDD
  }
}

database "SQLite database" as Database
folder "Local media storage" as Media

Student --> Presentation : browse
Lecturer --> Presentation : browse
Presentation --> Identity : authenticate
Presentation --> Courses : course pages
Presentation --> Learning : learning pages
Presentation --> AcademicRecord : later pages
Presentation --> Registration : later pages
Presentation --> Finance : later pages
Presentation --> StudentServices : later pages

Learning --> Identity : authenticated user
Learning --> Courses : enrollment and teaching checks
Learning --> Database : assignments, submissions, feedback
Learning --> Media : assignment files

AcademicRecord ..> Identity : later: user access
AcademicRecord ..> Courses : later: course context
Registration ..> Identity : later: user access
Registration ..> Courses : later: offerings and enrollment request
Registration ..> AcademicRecord : later: prerequisite results
Finance ..> Identity : later: user access
Finance ..> Courses : later: enrollment context
Finance ..> Registration : later: approved registration outcome
StudentServices ..> Identity : later: user access
StudentServices ..> Courses : later: course context

Identity --> Database : users and roles
Courses --> Database : courses and enrollments

legend right
  Solid components and arrows: first-release structure.
  Gray components and dashed arrows: future roadmap scope.
  Modules own their records and do not write directly to another module's records.
endlegend
@enduml
